// F93: round 1 of the 2026-10-12 benchmark had `for i in 1..=20` answered with "expected an
// expression, found '='" plus a bogus "expected 'fn'" on the next line, and four later runs across
// rounds 2 and the variance wave avoided ranges altogether rather than risk an off-by-one the
// compiler would not settle -- one wrote "`--check` alone cannot distinguish the two". The exclusive
// end has been in docs/SYNTAX.md all along; a program being measured cannot read it, so the
// diagnostic says it. Reporting this in the lexer is also what ends the cascade.
fn main() {
    for i in 1..=20 {
        print(i)
    }
}
